    "ssky_faqs_hgN78D": {
      "type": "ssky-faqs",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_MdKRCN": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "<p>Frequently Asked Questions About Books for Kids Aged 5 to 8</p>",
            "heading_size": "h1",
            "heading_weight": "bold"
          }
        },
        "faq_WRG3Up": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>What Types of Books Are Best for 5- To 8-Year-Olds?</p>",
            "text_size": "medium",
            "text_weight": "bold",
            "answer": "<p>Parents often want to know which formats and genres are most suitable. At this age, children are typically ready for a mix of:</p><ul><li>Picture books (for ages 5–6)</li><li>Early readers/leveled readers (for ages 6–7)</li><li>Short chapter books (for ages 7–8)</li></ul><p>Popular genres include adventure, humor, fantasy, and stories about friendship or school life.</p>",
            "text_size_b": "medium",
            "text_weight_b": "regular"
          }
        },
        "faq_qbCTw7": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>How Can I Tell if a Book Is at the Right Reading Level for My Child?</p>",
            "text_size": "medium",
            "text_weight": "bold",
            "answer": "<p>Parents may be unsure if a book is too hard or too easy. Common tips include:</p><ul><li>The \"Five Finger Rule\" (if a child struggles with 5+ words on a page, it might be too difficult)</li><li>Looking for leveled readers (e.g., Level 1, Level 2)</li><li>Consulting Lexile scores, AR levels, or publisher recommendations for age ranges.</li></ul>",
            "text_size_b": "medium",
            "text_weight_b": "regular"
          }
        },
        "faq_LizneF": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>How Do I Keep My Child Interested in Reading?</p>",
            "text_size": "medium",
            "text_weight": "bold",
            "answer": "<p>Parents often ask how to nurture their children’s love for books. Strategies include:</p><ul><li>Letting kids choose their own books</li><li>Reading aloud together</li><li>Offering book series with recurring characters</li><li>Mixing fiction with nonfiction on topics the child is interested in (e.g., animals, space)</li></ul>",
            "text_size_b": "medium",
            "text_weight_b": "regular"
          }
        },
        "faq_ENmNMp": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Are There Any Books That Promote Emotional or Social Development?</p>",
            "text_size": "medium",
            "text_weight": "bold",
            "answer": "<p>Yes, many parents seek books that help children understand emotions, empathy, and relationships. Some examples include books about making friends, resolving conflict, or handling big feelings.</p>",
            "text_size_b": "medium",
            "text_weight_b": "regular"
          }
        },
        "faq_jFAykq": {
          "type": "faq",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Are There Diverse and Inclusive Books for Kids in This Age Group?</p>",
            "text_size": "medium",
            "text_weight": "bold",
            "answer": "<p>As parents, we want books that vary in culture, background, and experiences so our children develop empathy and tolerance. Luckily, there are amazing books available for children that feature:</p><ul><li>Characters of different races, ethnicities, and family structures.</li><li>Stories that highlight disabilities, neurodiversity, or gender expression.</li><li>Books that celebrate cultural traditions from around the world.</li></ul>",
            "text_size_b": "medium",
            "text_weight_b": "regular"
          }
        },
        "faq_X696LK": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Looking for Something Else?</p>",
            "text_size": "medium",
            "text_weight": "bold",
            "answer": "<p>No matter their age, there's a Tuttle Twins product designed to spark curiosity and inspire confidence in your little one. Start your child’s journey toward independent thinking today with our <a href=\"https://tuttletwins.com/products/americas-history-volume-1-2-bundle\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">America’s history</span></a> and <a href=\"https://tuttletwins.com/products/the-tuttle-twins-learn-about-the-law\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">law</span></a> books. We also have <a href=\"https://tuttletwins.com/pages/books-for-teens\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">books for teens</span></a> that will engage their minds.</p>",
            "text_size_b": "medium",
            "text_weight_b": "regular"
          }
        }
      },
